  "term": "cachexia",
  "definition": "Cachexia is a complex syndrome marked by loss of muscle and body weight, seen here in the context of cancer and chemotherapy. In this source, it is described as often not improving with nutritional support and as involving reduced muscle protein content and protein building in skeletal muscle.",
